maluos-agent (0.5.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The personal agent: the desk token and the desk key are granted to it
    to read for a week (maluctl secret grant --level read), not delegated
    use-only: it presents the token to the office and signs envelopes with
    the key itself, and the vault hands a use-only value to brokers alone
    (use_requires_broker). It reads them with mode read.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:12:52 +0000

maluos-agent (0.5.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 2, delegation (docs/phase13-slice2-delegation.md): the
    task interface verifies the envelope on tasks/send against the
    directory's keys (/run/maluos/estate/keys.json), its expiry and nonce,
    and applies the agent's own policy (/etc/maluos/agents/NAME.policy.yaml:
    accept_from, max_classification, approve); a task the policy wants
    approved parks as pending_approval until tasks/resume brings the
    person's signed decision; the task record carries provenance (the
    chain, the model calls made) and usage; the estate daemon may bring an
    envelope-bearing task over the socket.  gateway_headers() and
    record_model_call() for agents' model calls.
  * maluctl agent create: --capability, --accept-from, --max-classification,
    --approve, --personal; the manifest the node registers in the directory
    (NAME.manifest.yaml) and the policy file; maluctl agent policy;
    maluctl agent personal renew; the hint /run/maluos/estate/agents-changed
    after create, remove and policy.
  * maluos-agent-personal.py: the person's own agent ("ask NAME …" sends a
    task with the person's envelope signed by the desk key).
  * Depends on maluos-estate (>= 0.3.0) for the envelope module.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:10:00 +0000

maluos-agent (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 9: answers stream. A task handler gets
    task["progress"](text) and the partial text rides in the task's
    output while it works; Client.stream() sends without waiting and
    polls tasks/get; `maluctl agent send` prints the answer as it grows.
    The demo agent reports "working on: …" before it asks the gateway.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:06:51 +0000

maluos-agent (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The task interface (Phase 12 slice 8): maluos_agent_tasks, JSON-RPC
    shaped like A2A (agent/card, tasks/send, tasks/get, tasks/list) on the
    agent's socket /run/maluos/agents/NAME/tasks.sock (the unit's runtime
    directory; MALUOS_AGENT_TASKS_SOCKET), admitting the owner, root and
    the agent by peer credentials. The demo agent serves it (each task is
    a question to the gateway). `maluctl agent card|send|tasks NAME` and
    `maluctl agent list --json`.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

maluos-agent (0.2.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Desk enrolment (Phase 12 slice 6): every maluos-agent@ unit and
    `maluctl agent run` load /etc/maluos/office.env when it exists, so
    agents see the office's endpoints (MALUOS_OFFICE_*) once the desk is
    enrolled.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000

maluos-agent (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Ownership (Phase 12 slice 3): `--owner user:NAME` (default: the sudo
    user when enrolled; `--owner none` for a system agent). Recorded in
    the registry maluos_agent (maluos-vault 0.3.0 schema) and as
    MALUOS_AGENT_OWNER in the agent's env file; a polkit rule in
    /etc/polkit-1/rules.d lets the owner's session start, stop and restart
    the unit. list and show print the owner; remove retires the row and the
    rule.

